| S9 | 936 | `Line 3057 (`cpu->cd.sh.fpul = (int32_t) op1.f;`) appears to be a copy-paste remnant from `X(fcnvds_drm_fpul)` directly below (`:3065-3075`), where writing `cpu->cd.sh.fpul` IS the instruction's output.` | `git show 987cb596:src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c`: line `3057` is `cpu->cd.sh.fpul = (int32_t) op1.f;`; lines `3065-3075` are `X(fcnvds_drm_fpul)`. |
| S10 | 936 | `(a) for any `|FPUL| <= 2^24` (where `float` is exact) and for `-2147483648` (`-2^31` is an exact power of two in `float`), `(int32_t) op1.f == (int32_t) fpul`, so `FPUL` happens to be overwritten with its own value and the bug is silent;` | Mathematical identity and verified in [witness_head.out:2-4](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/shfcnvsdfpul/witness_20261102/witness_head.out#L2-L4). |
| S11 | 936 | `(b) for any 32-bit integer with more than 24 significant bits between the leading and trailing 1 (`|FPUL| > 2^24` and not a multiple of the local `float` ULP), `(float)(int32_t) fpul` rounds to 24 mantissa bits before `store_64bit_in_fp_reg` converts `op1.f` to double (#575 tracks that precision loss separately), AND line 3057 then writes the rounded `float` back into `FPUL` as `(int32_t) op1.f`, destroying the low bits of `FPUL`;` | Verified by `987cb596:src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c:3056-3061` and [witness_head.out:2-5](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/shfcnvsdfpul/witness_20261102/witness_head.out#L2-L5). |
| S12 | 936 | `(c) for `FPUL in [0x7fffff80, 0x7fffffff]` (`2147483520 .. 2147483647`, 128 values), `(float)(int32_t) fpul` rounds up to `+2147483648.0f = +2^31`, which is out of `int32_t` range -- `(int32_t) op1.f` is C99 6.3.1.4p1 undefined behaviour (on x86-64 `cvttss2si` it yields the indefinite integer `0x80000000`, flipping `FPUL` from `+2147483647` to `-2147483648`).` | Verified by [witness_head.out:2-6](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/shfcnvsdfpul/witness_20261102/witness_head.out#L2-L6) (`0x7fffff80..0x7fffffff` = 128 values; `0x7fffffff -> 0x80000000`). |
| S13 | 938 | `**Standalone witness (`regress/artifacts/shfcnvsdfpul/witness_20261102/`).** `sh_fcnvsd_witness.py` boots a minimal SH-4 (`testsh`) machine at `PC = 0x8c001000` with `FPSCR = 0x00080000` (`PR=1, SZ=0, FR=0, RM=0`)` | [sh_fcnvsd_witness.py:21-83](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/shfcnvsdfpul/witness_20261102/sh_fcnvsd_witness.py#L21-L83) (`ENTRY = 0x8C001000`, `0x00080000`, `-E testsh`). |
